        "bug_id": "BUG-001",
        "title": "OOB_SIGNEDNESS_MISMATCH_IN_INDEX_VALIDATION",
        "root_cause": {
          "type": "Signedness Error",
          "description": "edit_cookie and read_cookie read the cookie index via scanf with format %llu (unsigned 64-bit), but validate it against cookie_num using a signed comparison (cmp rdx,rax; jl). The jl instruction performs a signed less-than comparison. An unsigned input with the high bit set (e.g. 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF, which is -1 in signed interpretation) will pass the 'index < cookie_num' check because -1 < 5 (or any positive cookie_num). There is no lower-bound check on the index. The attacker-controlled index is then used to compute addresses into the msg[] pointer array (msg + index*8) and msg_size[] int array (msg_size + index*4), enabling out-of-bounds array access."
        },
        "affected_functions": [
          "edit_cookie",
          "read_cookie"
        ],
        "affected_objects": [
          "msg[32] @0x4060 (char* array, 256 bytes)",
          "msg_size[32] @0x4160 (int array, 128 bytes)",
          "cookie_num @0x41e8 (long)"
        ],
        "attack_surface": {
          "input": "cookie index via scanf %llu (unsigned 64-bit)",
          "entry_function": "edit_cookie / read_cookie",
          "data_flow": [
            "scanf('%llu', &index) stores unsigned 64-bit value into rbp-0x10",
            "index loaded into rdx at 0x1676 (edit) / 0x179f (read)",
            "cookie_num loaded into rax at 0x167a (edit) / 0x17a3 (read)",
            "cmp rdx,rax at 0x1681 (edit) / 0x17aa (read): compares index and cookie_num as 64-bit values",
            "jl at 0x1684 (edit) / 0x17ad (read): signed jump-if-less — treats both operands as signed",
            "If index has high bit set (>= 0x8000000000000000), it is negative in signed interpretation and passes the < cookie_num check",
            "In edit_cookie: index used at 0x16a7 (lea rdx,[rax*4]) to compute msg_size+index*4 for read length, and at 0x16c3 (lea rcx,[rax*8]) to compute msg+index*8 for read destination pointer",
            "In read_cookie: index used at 0x17bf (lea rdx,[rax*8]) to compute msg+index*8 for pointer dereference, then printf('%s', msg[index])"
          ]
        },
        "security_check": {
          "expected": "Index should be validated as an unsigned value in range [0, cookie_num-1], using unsigned comparison (jb/jae) and checking both lower bound (>= 0) and upper bound (< cookie_num).",
          "actual": "Index is read as unsigned %llu but compared with signed jl instruction. Only upper bound is checked (via signed comparison). No lower bound check exists.",
          "missing_or_incorrect": "Missing lower-bound check AND incorrect comparison type: signed jl used instead of unsigned jb. The signedness mismatch allows negative-valued (high-bit-set) unsigned inputs to bypass the upper bound check."
