            "type": "OOB_READ",
            "status": "CANDIDATE",
            "reason": "In both edit_cookie and read_cookie, the attacker-controlled index causes OOB read from the msg[] array (at msg+index*8). The value read from OOB memory is treated as a pointer. In read_cookie, this pointer is passed to printf('%s', ptr), causing dereference and string output — potential information disclosure of memory contents at the OOB-derived pointer address. In edit_cookie, OOB reads from both msg[] and msg_size[] arrays obtain a pointer and a size value from out-of-bounds memory."
