          "type": "Integer Underflow",
          "description": "create_cookie allows msg_len=0 because the check 'cmp rax,0x100; jle' (at 0x13f6-0x13fc) uses signed jle, and 0 <= 0x100 passes. When msg_len=0, calloc(0,1) allocates a minimum-size heap chunk, and msg_size[cookie_num] is set to 0 (stored as int at 0x14a9). When edit_cookie is later called on this cookie, it computes the read length as msg_size[index]-1. The instruction sequence 'mov eax, [msg_size+index*4]; sub eax,0x1; movsxd rdx,eax' (at 0x16b6-0x16bc) performs 0-1 on a 32-bit int, producing -1 (0xFFFFFFFF), then sign-extends to 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF as the 64-bit size argument to read(). This causes read(0, msg[index], 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF), attempting to read an enormous number of bytes into a small heap buffer."
