          "type": "Use-After-Free",
          "description": "eat_cookie frees msg[random_index] at 0x158e, then copies msg[cookie_num-1] into msg[random_index] at 0x15c6. When random_index equals cookie_num-1 (i.e., the last cookie is selected for eating), the sequence is: free(msg[cookie_num-1]); msg[cookie_num-1] = msg[cookie_num-1] (writes the freed pointer back to the same slot). The slot now holds a dangling pointer to freed heap memory. cookie_num is decremented, but the old msg[cookie_num-1] slot (now at index cookie_num, which is 'beyond' the active range) is NOT zeroed. The dangling pointer at msg[random_index] (= msg[old_cookie_num-1]) remains accessible if the same index can be reached again. However, after cookie_num decrement, the dangling pointer is at index cookie_num (the old cookie_num-1), which is now outside the valid range [0, cookie_num-1]. Accessing it requires either the signedness bug (BUG-001) to bypass the index check, or creating new cookies to fill the slot."
