            "root_cause": "Signedness mismatch in index validation: edit_cookie and read_cookie read index via scanf %llu (unsigned 64-bit) but validate with signed jl comparison. An unsigned value with high bit set (e.g. 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFC = -4 signed) passes the < cookie_num check, enabling OOB access to BSS data before the msg[] array.",
            "description": "read_cookie with negative index -4 (0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFC) accesses msg[-4] at address 0x4040, which holds the stderr FILE* pointer (libc address). This pointer is dereferenced by printf('%s', msg[index]), leaking bytes from the FILE structure in libc memory."
          },
          "chain": [
            "BUG-001",
            "Signedness mismatch: %llu input + signed jl comparison",
            "Negative index -4 bypasses index < cookie_num check",
            "msg[-4] at 0x4040 = stderr FILE* pointer (libc address)",
            "printf('%s', stderr_ptr) dereferences and prints FILE structure bytes",
            "INFO_LEAK"
          ],
          "controlled_element": {
            "what": "Index value passed to read_cookie via scanf %llu",
            "how": "Attacker sends unsigned representation of -4 (0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFC) as the cookie index. The signed jl comparison treats this as -4 < 5 (cookie_num), passing the check. The index is used to compute msg + (-4)*8 = 0x4060 - 32 = 0x4040, which is the stderr FILE* global.",
