              "necessity": "Without bypassing the index check, no OOB access occurs. The signed jl treats high-bit-set values as negative, which is always < positive cookie_num.",
              "verified": true
            },
            {
              "id": "PC-02",
              "description": "The OOB slot msg[-4] at 0x4040 must contain a valid (non-NULL) pointer to readable memory",
              "necessity": "printf('%s', ptr) dereferences the pointer. If NULL or unmapped, SIGSEGV occurs instead of info leak. stderr FILE* is initialized by init() via setvbuf, so it points to a valid libc FILE structure.",
              "verified": true
            },
            {
              "id": "PC-03",
              "description": "cookie_num must be > 0 (at least one cookie exists) for the index check to have a positive comparison value",
              "necessity": "If cookie_num=0, the jl comparison would be index < 0, and even negative indices would fail. init() sets cookie_num=5, satisfying this.",
